Dear distance users,

I'm having a problem with the predict function in mrds package, and I'm sure somebody here can help me :)
I need to obtain the detection probabilities for a new set of distances (say from 0 to 40000m, by 100m intervals, in the following example) but when I use the predict function on a new dataframe I only obtain a vector with the same average value of detection probability (that I already had, in the model summary), repeated 400 times.
What am I doing wrong?

newdata <- data.frame(distance=seq(0,40000,100))
pred<-predict(my.ds.model$ddf, type="state", newdata=newdata)

Many thanks in advance for any help!

